/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  landscape07_sugar_nitrogen_all_pathways
  =======================================
  TWO GIBBS MAPS THAT CARRY A PURE SOLID, the first cases to (2026-09-29).
  Until that day `gibbsMap` called the fluid-only solve, so a species whose
  record declares `referenceState pureSolid;` was priced on the ideal-gas
  rung and its record refused the whole map (found by Vitor, mapping
  sucrose beside the gases).  The op now calls `GibbsMethod::solve`, the one
  home the gibbsReactor already used: a declared pure solid is its own
  phase at activity one, deposited only where the solid-free equilibrium
  would supersaturate it, and its amount is the CSV column `s_<name>`.

  sugarNitrogen -- the REACTANTS of the sucrose nitrogen-fixation route
      C12H22O11(s) + 8 N2 + 13 H2O  ->  12 CO2 + 16 NH3
  (balanced by electron count; its dG at 298.15 K, 1 bar is about -355 kJ
  per sucrose on `reactionGibbs`, so the ROUTE is permitted), handed to a
  Gibbs map with every species open, methane included.  Where the atoms
  go at minimum G is NOT that route: measured, the carbon ends as methane
  and CO2 (the anaerobic digester's answer), the nitrogen stays N2 and
  ammonia is near 1e-6 at ambient.  A declared route that is permitted is
  not the route equilibrium picks; the organism picks it with an enzyme.

  boudouard -- 2 CO <-> C(graphite) + CO2, CO fed alone: carbon DEPOSITS
  at low temperature and not at high, pinned as the fraction of the fed
  carbon that leaves as graphite (elementYield on the solid).

  NOT HERE, said: a solid that must REMAIN for the atoms to close.  With
  the six species sucrose, CO2, N2, NH3, H2, water and no methane, carbon
  has one fluid carrier (CO2) and too little oxygen for it, so the
  solid-free equilibrium the solid test starts from does not exist; every
  cell reports unconverged, with the solver's own cause printed.  That is a
  limit of GibbsMethod::solve, the same in the gibbsReactor, recorded in
  DEV.md section 5, not fixed here.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name      sugarNitrogen;
        type      gibbsMap;
        elements  ( C H O N );
        species
        (
            { name sucrose;  atoms ( 12 22 11 0 ); }
            { name N2;       atoms ( 0 0 0 2 ); }
            { name water;    atoms ( 0 2 1 0 ); }
            { name CO2;      atoms ( 1 0 2 0 ); }
            { name NH3;      atoms ( 0 3 0 1 ); }
            { name H2;       atoms ( 0 2 0 0 ); }
            { name CH4;      atoms ( 1 4 0 0 ); }
        );
        feed      { sucrose 1; N2 8; water 13; }
        Tgrid     { from 298.15; to 598.15; n 13; }          // K
        Pgrid     { from 1.0e5; to 1.0e7; n 3; log true; }   // Pa: 1, 10, 100 bar
        metric    { type moleFraction; species NH3; }
        anchors
        (
            { T 298.15; P 101325; }    // ambient: 25 C, 1 atm
            { T 310.15; P 101325; }    // body temperature
        );
        output    { file sugarNitrogen.csv; }
    }
    {
        name      boudouard;
        type      gibbsMap;
        elements  ( C O );
        species
        (
            { name CO;        atoms ( 1 1 ); }
            { name CO2;       atoms ( 1 2 ); }
            { name graphite;  atoms ( 1 0 ); }
        );
        feed      { CO 2; }
        Tgrid     { from 600; to 1300; n 15; }               // K
        Pgrid     { from 1.0e5; to 1.0e6; n 2; log true; }   // Pa: 1, 10 bar
        metric    { type elementYield; product graphite; element C; }
        anchors
        (
            { T 700;  P 101325; }      // deposits
            { T 1200; P 101325; }      // does not
        );
        output    { file boudouard.csv; }
    }
);
